# __TITLE__

__DESCRIPTION__

This plugin was scaffolded as a __KIND__ plugin. It holds one skill (`skills/__SKILL__/SKILL.md`) and its tests.
Replace the placeholder text, keep the tests green, and run the checks before every release.

## Where it works

| Surface | What loads |
|---|---|
| Claude Code (terminal, IDE) | everything in this plugin |
| Claude Desktop, Code tab and Cowork | skills, agents, hooks, remote and local MCP servers |
| claude.ai chat (web, mobile) | skills, and remote MCP servers as connectors; hooks and local servers are ignored |
| Claude for Office add-ins | skills enabled in your Claude settings |
| Agent SDK | the plugin folder, loaded by path |

Surfaces this plugin was built for: __SURFACES__. A top-level `bin/` folder would make claude.ai refuse the whole
plugin, so executables live in `scripts/` instead.

## What runs on your machine
__RUNS_LOCALLY__

## Add it and develop it

```bash
claude plugin marketplace add <path or git URL of this repository>
claude plugin install __NAME__@<marketplace name>
claude --plugin-dir plugins/__NAME__        # load it for one session while you work
```

Run the rules check and the tests from the repository root:

```bash
python tools/check_plugin.py plugins/__NAME__
python -m unittest discover -s plugins/__NAME__/tests -v
```

See `SECURITY.md` for how to report a problem and `CHANGELOG.md` for what changed.
